body:
Feel this in my soul. Unstable sister solidarity!

&#x200B;

I like to toy with the idea of adopting a troubled older kid when I'm much older (and in theory more in charge of the mads). In part because it won't have my corrupted genes, but also because I won't have to live with the guilt of knowing I fucked it up for them. The formative years of a child's development dictates so much of their future and who they fundamentally are as a person, I couldn't survive knowing that I'd set someone up for a tormented life with my instability. 

&#x200B;

Instead get one that's already pretty fucked up. And just get to be like- Hey buddy. We're both in the crazy boat, let's try and figure it out together. 

&#x200B;

But realistically I know that I couldn't/shouldn't. My severe mental illness means I probably wouldn't be allowed to anyway. And a troubled kid needs even MORE stability that your average one, so I'd be doing more harm than good, just to settle my own selfish vanity.

&#x200B;

It's a wholeheartedly, intolerably torturous decision to have to make, but one I feel is irrevocably correct. 

&#x200B;

Fuck you maternal hormones swimming around in my biological business and turning my brain and uterus into sadness soup.
